# Tracer: runtime-local WD evidence stays in its owning Lean theorem.
#
# Before (Litex verified, but Lean scope was wrong):
# forall a, b R, g fn(x R) R, t fn(x R) R, f fn(x, y R) R:
#     f(g(a), t(b)) = f(g(a), t(b))
# Former behavior: generalized `wd_N`, `obj_N_applicable`, and `obj_N_result`
# declarations were emitted at the top level before the source theorem.
#
# Now (verified):
forall a, b R, g fn(x R) R, t fn(x R) R, f fn(x, y R) R:
    f(g(a), t(b)) = f(g(a), t(b))
# Current behavior: the theorem type uses proof-free `g [a]`, `t [b]`, and
# `f [g [a], t [b]]`. After `intro`, local `wd_0_N`, applicability, and result
# membership steps replay the verifier DAG in child-before-parent order.

# Boundary: this tracer covers one lexical forall environment. A child/local
# environment may see parent WD entries, but a closed environment's cache does
# not escape its scope. Function-valued bodyless `have`/`trust have` remains a
# separate To-Lean statement tranche and is not silently treated as this case.
# Evidence: `LITEX_LEAN_PROJECT=lean LITEX_LAKE=lake cargo test --release
# scoped_nested_object_aliases_compile_with_mathlib -- --ignored --nocapture`.
